# ─── Firebase Configuration ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Go to https://console.firebase.google.com
# 2. Create a project (or open an existing one)
# 3. Open Project Settings → General → Your apps → Web app
# 4. Click "Add app" (or select existing web app) to get these values
# 5. Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values below
#
# For Vercel deployment, add each variable in:
#   Vercel Dashboard → Project → Settings → Environment Variables

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ─── Firestore setup ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# After creating the Firebase project:
# 1. In Firebase Console → Build → Firestore Database → Create database
# 2. Choose "Start in production mode" (recommended) or "test mode"
# 3. Select a region close to your users
# 4. Deploy the security rules in firestore.rules:
#      npm install -g firebase-tools
#      firebase login
#      firebase use --add          # pick your project
#      firebase deploy --only firestore:rules
